  "query_preview": "..\n\nWEATHER PATTERN OVERVIEW:\nWith an upper trough over Montana, cooler conditions with clouds\nand scattered showers will continue. The next batch of showers\nwill move southeast through the CWA tonight bringing about a tenth\nof an inch to most areas. Lighter showers will linger Thursday\nnortheast of a Malta to Glendive line.\n\nThe main impact through the weekend for most will be the cool\ntemps expected. The upper low will drift east allowing a northerly\nflow to help drop nighttime temps into the 40s. Saturday night\nappears to be the coolest night with lows possibily dropping into\nthe 30s in many places. We will begin to message this with social\nmedia and possibly Weather Stories.\n\nOtherwise, weak disturbances will be moving through the area\nbringing scattered showers into the weekend.\n\nAn upper ridge building over western Canada this weekend will\ngradually flatten early next week but should provide some warming\nand drier conditions. Temps should recover to near normal. \n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS:\nTweaked pops closer to the CAMS/Near term models. NBM has been too\nlow with pops with current upper trough.\n\nConfidence then remains above average for the cool and unsettled \nweather to continue for next few days given the overall handling \nof the trough. Confidence in exact timing, placement, and amount \nof precipitation remains low to moderate given the mesoscale \ndetail still to be worked out a larger time scales.",
